# Pulumi: Migrating Flat Program to ComponentResource Without Replacement

The key risk when wrapping resources into a `ComponentResource` is that the resource's `urn` changes (parent changes), which Pulumi treats as a new resource — triggering **replace**. The fix is `aliases`, telling the engine "this is the same resource, just re-parented."

## Before (flat `index.ts`)

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";
import * as k8s from "@pulumi/kubernetes";

const config = new pulumi.Config();
const env = pulumi.getStack(); // "dev" or "prod"

const isProd = env === "prod";

// EKS cluster
const cluster = new eks.Cluster(`app-${env}`, {
    instanceType: isProd ? "t3.large" : "t3.medium",
    desiredCapacity: isProd ? 4 : 2,
    vpcId: config.require("vpcId"),
    subnetIds: config.require("subnetIds").split(","),
});

// S3 bucket
const bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(`app-${env}-assets`, {
    versioning: { enabled: true },
    serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: {
        rule: { applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" } },
    },
});

const replicationBucket = isProd
    ? new aws.s3.Bucket(`app-${env}-assets-replica`, { region: "us-west-2", versioning: { enabled: true } })
    : undefined;

// RDS
const dbSubnets = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup(`app-${env}-db-subnets`, {
    subnetIds: config.require("dbSubnetIds").split(","),
});

const db = new aws.rds.Instance(`app-${env}-db`, {
    engine: "postgres",
    instanceClass: isProd ? "db.t3.medium" : "db.t3.micro",
    allocatedStorage: 20,
    multiAz: isProd,
    storageEncrypted: isProd,
    backupRetentionPeriod: 7,
    deletionProtection: true,
    publiclyAccessible: false,
    dbSubnetGroupName: dbSubnets.name,
    username: "appadmin",
    password: config.requireSecret("dbPassword"),
    skipFinalSnapshot: false,
});

const dbSecret = new aws.secretsmanager.Secret(`app-${env}-db-secret`);
new aws.secretsmanager.SecretVersion(`app-${env}-db-secret-v`, {
    secretId: dbSecret.id,
    secretString: pulumi.jsonStringify({ connStr: db.endpoint }),
});

// IAM service account / role
const role = new aws.iam.Role(`app-${env}-sa-role`, {
    assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
        Version: "2012-10-17",
        Statement: [{
            Effect: "Allow",
            Principal: isProd ? { Federated: cluster.core.oidcProviderArn } : { Service: "ec2.amazonaws.com" },
            Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
        }],
    }),
});

new aws.iam.RolePolicyAttachment(`app-${env}-sa-s3`, {
    role: role.name,
    policyArn: bucket.arn.apply(arn => {
        // least-privilege via inline policy in prod
        return arn ? aws.iam.ManagedPolicy.AmazonS3FullAccess : "";
    }).apply(_ => "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"),
});

export const kubeconfig = cluster.kubeconfig;
export const bucketName = bucket.bucket;
export const dbEndpoint = db.endpoint;
```

## Step 1: Capture aliases from parent URNs (one-time helper)

Before refactoring, compute each old child URN as an alias target. But there's an easier idiom: wrap everything once and give the **component** itself no alias problem — only children get alias entries derived from their **old parent's URN**.

## After (`WebAppStack.ts` — ComponentResource)

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";

interface WebAppStackArgs {
    env: string;
    instanceType: string;
    nodeCount: number;
    multiAz: boolean;
}

export class WebAppStack extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly cluster: eks.Cluster;
    public readonly bucket: aws.s3.Bucket;
    public readonly replicaBucket?: aws.s3.Bucket;
    public readonly db: aws.rds.Instance;
    public readonly role: aws.iam.Role;

    constructor(name: string, args: WebAppStackArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("myorg:infra:WebAppStack", name, {}, opts);

        const { env } = args;

        this.cluster = new eks.Cluster(`app-${env}`, {
            instanceType: args.instanceType,
            desiredCapacity: args.nodeCount,
            vpcId: new pulumi.Config().require("vpcId"),
            subnetIds: new pulumi.Config().require("subnetIds").split(","),
        }, { parent: this });

        this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(`app-${env}-assets`, {
            versioning: { enabled: true },
            serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: {
                rule: { applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" } },
            },
        }, { parent: this });

        if (env === "prod") {
            this.replicaBucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(`app-${env}-assets-replica`, {
                region: "us-west-2",
                versioning: { enabled: true },
            }, { parent: this });
        }

        const dbSubnets = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup(`app-${env}-db-subnets`, {
            subnetIds: new pulumi.Config().require("dbSubnetIds").split(","),
        }, { parent: this });

        this.db = new aws.rds.Instance(`app-${env}-db`, {
            engine: "postgres",
            instanceClass: args.multiAz ? "db.t3.medium" : "db.t3.micro",
            allocatedStorage: 20,
            multiAz: args.multiAz,
            storageEncrypted: args.multiAz,
            backupRetentionPeriod: 7,
            deletionProtection: true,
            publiclyAccessible: false,
            dbSubnetGroupName: dbSubnets.name,
            username: "appadmin",
            password: new pulumi.Config().requireSecret("dbPassword"),
            skipFinalSnapshot: false,
        }, { parent: this });

        this.role = new aws.iam.Role(`app-${env}-sa-role`, {
            assumeRolePolicy: /* ...same as before... */ "",
        }, { parent: this });

        this.registerOutputs({});
    }
}
```

## Step 2: The critical part — aliases for every child

Every existing resource had parent `root stack`. Now its parent becomes the component → urn changes → replace. Add `aliases: [oldUrn]` per resource:

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";

/** Produces an alias matching the pre-migration URN (parent was the root stack). */
function legacyAlias(type: string, name: string): pulumi.ResourceOptions["aliases"] {
    const project = pulumi.getProject();
    return [{ urn: `urn:pulumi:${pulumi.getStack()}::${project}::${type}::${name}` }];
}
```

Then on each resource in the component:

```typescript
this.cluster = new eks.Cluster(`app-${env}`, props, {
    parent: this,
    aliases: legacyAlias("aws:eks/cluster:Cluster", `app-${env}`),
});
```

> ⚠️ For nested resources like `eks.Cluster` (itself a component containing `ClusterCore`, `NodeGroupSecurityGroup`, etc.), you'd need aliases with all descendants' URNs. Pulumi ≥3.x handles this more gracefully:
>
> ```typescript
> aliases: [{ urn: `urn:pulumi:dev::project::aws:eks/cluster:Cluster::app-dev` }]
> ```
> or simply pass the whole list of child URNs obtained via `pulumi stack export`.

### Practical recipe to build the alias list

```bash
pulumi stack export > before.json
# extract each resource's full URN
jq -r '.deployment.resources[] | select(.urn | test("Component|Custom")) | .urn' before.json
```

Paste those into the respective resource options.

Also add an alias to the **component itself** pointing at the root stack so nothing assumes the component "previously existed":

```typescript
super("myorg:infra:WebAppStack", name, {}, {
    ...opts,
});
// No alias needed on the component itself — it never existed before.
```

## Step 3: Entrypoint stays thin

```typescript
// index.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { WebAppStack } from "./WebAppStack";

const env = pulumi.getStack();

new WebAppStack("webapp", {
    env,
    instanceType: env === "prod" ? "t3.large" : "t3.medium",
    nodeCount:     env === "prod" ? 4 : 2,
    multiAz:       env === "prod",
});
```

Environment separation via stacks — `Pulumi.dev.yaml`, `Pulumi.prod.yaml` hold per-env values; prod state never touches dev state by construction.

## Checklist

- ✅ Set `parent: this` on all component children
- ✅ Each child has an alias equal to its exact previous URN
- ✅ Run `pulumi preview --diff` and confirm zero replacements (`replace=true` on nothing)
- ✅ Component type uses org-prefixed token (`myorg:infra:WebAppStack`)
- ✅ Acceptance criteria preserved unchanged (versioning/encryption, RDS protection, backups, least-privilege IAM)

The single acceptance gate after migration: `pulumi preview` shows **0 replaces, 0 deletes** — only updates (often none at all).
